    'Group skills development' => [
        'cat' => 'Life skills',
        'short' => 'Group skills development is skill-building delivered in a group, where people learn and practise together. Topics include communication, independence and social confidence.',
        'overview' => "Learning alongside others can make new skills feel less daunting. In a group, people see how others tackle the same challenge, practise together and give and receive encouragement. Programs are usually led by a support worker, therapist or trainer, and run over a series of sessions with a clear focus.\n\nCommon topics include communication and social skills, cooking, managing money, travelling independently, health and wellbeing, and preparing for work or study. Some programs are for a particular age group or interest, such as young adults leaving school, which makes the content more relevant.\n\nA good group balances structure with flexibility. Leaders explain what will be covered, set activities at different levels and check how each person is going, so no one is left behind or held back. It is worth asking how progress is tracked and what happens once the program finishes.",
        'choose' => [
