        'overview' => "An audiologist is a health professional who specialises in hearing and balance. A hearing assessment measures how well you hear sounds at different pitches and volumes and how well you understand speech. The results guide advice about management, which might include devices, communication strategies, protection from noise or referral to a doctor or specialist.\n\nAudiologists also help with related conditions, including tinnitus, which is hearing a sound that is not there, and some balance problems. Children can have their hearing tested from a very young age, and early detection helps with speech and learning.\n\nHearing changes over time, so regular check-ups make sense, especially if you notice changes, use hearing devices or are exposed to loud noise. Ask the clinic what to expect at your first visit and how they explain results in plain language.",
