    'Individualised Living Options (ILO)' => [
        'cat' => 'Housing (SDA & SIL)',
        'short' => 'An Individualised Living Option is a way of designing where and how you live around your own goals and preferences, instead of choosing from existing housing models.',
        'overview' => "Most people think of housing as a choice between living at home with family and moving into a shared home run by a provider. Individualised Living Options open up other possibilities, such as living in your own place with tailored support, sharing with a housemate you choose or living alongside family in a way that gives everyone more freedom.\n\nThe process usually has stages. First there is exploration, where you think about what you want your life to look like and who is important to you. Then comes design, where a provider or coordinator helps you shape a living arrangement and the supports that will make it work. Finally, the arrangement is set up and reviewed as you settle in.\n\nBecause ILO is a newer and more personal approach, it helps to ask providers about their experience and how they involve you. A good provider listens, explains options in plain language and moves at a pace that suits you and your family.",
